WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.419
Let's go next to our caller from the six five
zero area code.

00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:07.599
Who's calling today from six five zero?

00:00:07.599 --> 00:00:10.530
Hi, David, this is so great.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.530
Hey, how's it.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.530
What's going on?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.870
And it hasn't gone on good.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.220
So I'm an international student from from
Mexico.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:26.880
Yeah, I was just wondering whether you managed
to see the new ruling from the Trump administration

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.029
that is just making it pretty hard for international
students.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:32.870
Get back in the states.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:33.870
Yeah.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.380
Most universities bend over backwards.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.080
So I did see it.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.220
I did see it.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.160
I'm I'm against the ruling.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:50.920
If you know, how can it be that it's safe
enough to open all elementary and high schools

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:57.570
and yet it is too dangerous to allow a relatively
modest number of international students to

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.570
come in?

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.570
It strikes me as discriminatory.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.970
Like, either it's safe to do schools or it's
not as my take.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:09.659
But I heard and I've not read a lot into this,
you maybe know more about this than I do that

00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:17.010
if schools say that they've assigned an individual
teacher to you for in-person learning, which

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:22.200
can just be like a five minute check in per
week, that technically then the students would

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.200
be allowed to come in.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.590
Have you heard anything about that?

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:26.840
Yes.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:35.710
So we basically have like we have to take
a certain number of credit hours as in person

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.090
or like hybrid.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.090
Right.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.549
In order for us to be able to take like the
rest of our course load online.

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:45.830
Yeah, it I mean, it just seems to have a lot
of loopholes in it.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:51.479
And to me, it just seems like a strategy to
get the schools to reopen forcibly, because

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:58.740
I just I mean, I'm studying computer science
and like I can't imagine the computer science

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:03.999
department at my university operating without
international students right there.

00:02:03.999 --> 00:02:11.220
The teacher is they are at like they weren't
student officers like I did.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.220
Yeah.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.160
It's just it's very draconian.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.630
It seems counterproductive.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:21.640
Well, it seems to me that either way, it will
give the Trump the Trump administration something

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.650
that they like.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.260
Either they will keep keep a bunch of foreigners
out.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.260
That's one possibility.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.390
And they would welcome that or it would get
schools to reopen even when they don't really

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.000
think it's the right thing to do, which is
also what the Trump administration wants.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.420
So it's almost like they're going to get something
they like out of this.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.670
No, I agreed.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:45.230
What did you think of the end game of of opening
schools?

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:49.200
It just seems like a bomb ready to explode
like you've done.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.250
You have a bunch of cases, right?

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.560
A visual household.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.060
You send all the kids to the same place to
infecting them.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.300
They all go back home to their parents and
get them infected.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:05.950
Yeah, I think we I think basically the hope
is the bomb won't go off until after November

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:06.950
3rd.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.270
Like, I think the calculation is schools won't.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:13.730
I believe that no schools open earlier than
late August here in Massachusetts.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:14.860
It's usually September.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.870
I think there's some states that open earlier.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:22.580
I think the calculation is if we get schools
open, we get the publicity of schools being

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.620
open.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.030
Parents are able to go back to their jobs,
maybe because they're not home watching their

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.060
kids.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:36.240
So the economy will show some better jobs
numbers and hopefully it'll all stay relatively

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.290
under control until November 3rd and it'll
get Trump reelected.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.290
I don't think it'll work.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:45.230
I mean, if you look at we it's right now as
we're filming this, it's the early afternoon.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.800
We already are at twenty five thousand new
cases today.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.330
It's only halfway through the day.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.580
Most states don't report until the afternoon.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.990
It seems like it's not going to work.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.621
But I think that's their idea.

00:03:55.621 --> 00:04:00.600
I don't think it's going to work.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.920
It's crazy.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:02.920
It's crazy.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:03.920
All right, my friend.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.000
I hope it works out.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.130
And I appreciate you letting me know what's
going on.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.590
Been you.

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:09.590
OK.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:10.590
Take care.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:11.590
Likewise.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:12.700
The pleasure is all on this side of the microphone.

